From: ClauCoDillo NuttX port
Subject: [PATCH] mwin: give mouse and keyboard independent per-cycle event budgets

MwSelect()'s polling-platform implementation (src/mwin/winmain.c)
drained mouse and keyboard input through two separate `while` loops,
but both shared a single `numevents` counter capped at 10. A burst of
mouse activity (rapid physical mouse movement, or a flood of X11
MotionNotify events) filling that shared counter left little or no
budget for the keyboard loop that runs immediately after it in the
same MwSelect() call, and vice versa: a held key's X11 auto-repeat
burst could starve mouse servicing.

Found investigating a real, live-reproduced bug: Backspace, which
users naturally hold down to delete several characters (generating a
fast X11 auto-repeat press stream), would reliably lose its key-down
events whenever mouse activity was also queued in the same cycle,
leaving only the trailing key-up once the backlog was finally
serviced. cfltk's Fl_Input widget only acts on key-down for
Backspace, so this presented as "Backspace silently does nothing."

Fix: give mouse and keyboard their own independent counters
(mouseevents, kbdevents), each still capped at 10 per MwSelect() call
as before, so neither can starve the other. `numevents` (used only to
decide whether to sleep afterward) is reconstructed as their sum,
preserving the original behavior for callers.

Note: this is a real, independently-justified fix, but it did not by
itself resolve a separate, more severe bug also found in the same
investigation -- an intermittent, genuine infinite-loop 100% CPU hang
triggered by rapid mouse movement in the full ClauCoDillo browser.
That hang is still unresolved; see docs/analysis.md and this
project's memory notes for what's been ruled out so far.

--- a/src/mwin/winmain.c
+++ b/src/mwin/winmain.c
@@ -418,25 +418,40 @@
 /* this MwSelect() is used for all polling-based platforms not specially handled above*/
 #define WAITTIME	50		/* blocking sleep interval in msecs unless polling*/
 
-void 
+void
 MwSelect(BOOL canBlock)
 {
 	int numevents = 0;
+	int mouseevents = 0;
+	int kbdevents = 0;
 
 	/* perform single update of aggregate screen update region*/
 	if (scrdev.PreSelect)
 		scrdev.PreSelect(&scrdev);
 
-	/* poll for mouse data and service if found*/
+	/* poll for mouse data and service if found. Mouse and keyboard each
+	 * get their own independent budget (not a single shared "numevents"
+	 * counter) -- a burst of mouse motion (rapid physical movement, or
+	 * X11 MotionNotify flooding) filling a shared counter would starve
+	 * keyboard servicing for the rest of this call, and vice versa for
+	 * a held key's X11 auto-repeat burst. Confirmed as a real bug this
+	 * way: Backspace (routinely held to delete several characters,
+	 * generating a fast X11 auto-repeat press burst) would reliably
+	 * lose its key-down events while mouse activity was also queued,
+	 * leaving only the trailing key-up once the backlog was finally
+	 * serviced -- Fl_Input's own handle_key() only acts on key-down,
+	 * so held Backspace silently did nothing. */
 	while (MwCheckMouseEvent())
-		if (++numevents > 10)
+		if (++mouseevents > 10)
 			break;				/* don't handle too many events at one shot*/
-	
+
 	/* poll for keyboard data and service if found*/
 	while (MwCheckKeyboardEvent())
-		if (++numevents > 10)
+		if (++kbdevents > 10)
 			break;				/* don't handle too many events at one shot*/
-	
+
+	numevents = mouseevents + kbdevents;
+
 #if MW_FEATURE_TIMERS
 	/* check for timer timeouts and service if found*/
 	if (GdTimeout())
